e first-term Republican Tom Barrett faces Democrat William Lawrence in a closely watched rematch-style contest. Expert raters are split: several call it a tossup, while a growing group of late-September ratings lean toward a Democratic flip. Prediction markets price Lawrence modestly ahead, around a 56-58 percent chance. The one recent poll, conducted for Democratic sponsors in mid-August, showed Lawrence up two points, though polling here is thin and aging. Barrett holds a decisive financial advantage, with $2.9 million on hand versus roughly $0.4 million for Lawrence, but Democrats and outside groups have spent heavily against the incumbent. Headlines highlight Barrett's effort to distance himself from some Trump positions while defending his district record. The race remains genuinely competitive, with a slight Democratic tilt heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}]}